<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Chocolatey package for NextFix. It downloads the signed installer from the GitHub release
  rather than embedding it, so there is exactly one binary that is "the NextFix installer" and
  every channel points at it. Version, URL and checksum are filled from the staged installer by
  packaging/windows/refresh-manifests.mjs; do not edit the generated copy by hand.
-->
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>nextfix</id>
    <version>1.1.0</version>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/GRCSAC/nextfix/tree/main/packaging/windows/manifests/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <owners>GRCSAC</owners>

    <title>NextFix</title>
    <authors>GRCSAC</authors>
    <projectUrl>https://nextfix.grcsac.com</projectUrl>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://github.com/GRCSAC/nextfix</projectSourceUrl>
    <!-- Chocolatey moderation rejects raw.githubusercontent.com icons; jsDelivr serves the file from the release tag. -->
    <iconUrl>https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/GRCSAC/nextfix@v1.1.0/packaging/icons/nextfix-256.png</iconUrl>
    <copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 GRCSAC LLC</copyright>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/GRCSAC/nextfix/blob/main/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <docsUrl>https://github.com/GRCSAC/nextfix#readme</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/GRCSAC/nextfix/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/GRCSAC/nextfix/releases/tag/v1.1.0</releaseNotes>
    <tags>nextfix security vulnerability vulnerability-management sca sbom vex sarif reachability devsecops appsec cve cli</tags>

    <summary>Tells you which of an application's vulnerabilities to fix next, and why. Scanners find. NextFix decides.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
NextFix looks at an application and tells you which of its vulnerabilities actually matter, in
what order, and why. Scanners already find thousands of issues; NextFix works out which ones are
**reachable** from an entry point, **exposed** to an attacker and **exploited** in the wild, and
hands both the executive and the engineer a short list with the evidence attached.

Point it at a Node.js, Python or Go project, or a container image, from the command line
(`nextfix scan .`), or start the local dashboards with `nextfix serve`. Reports come out as JSON,
OpenVEX and SARIF for CI gates and GitHub code scanning. It runs entirely on your own machine or
server; nothing leaves your network. Apache-2.0.

### Install scope

The installer is **per-user**: it needs no administrator rights, installs into
`%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\NextFix` and adds that folder to the user's PATH. Chocolatey normally
runs from an elevated shell, so NextFix is installed for **the account running `choco install`**,
not for every user on the machine.

Scan history, accounts and settings live in `%USERPROFILE%\.nextfix` and are kept on uninstall.
    ]]></description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
